{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>אך.</b> The wise men, the counselors of — so the grammar is: the wise men of Pharaoh, the counselors of Pharaoh. It is an elliptical form. Likewise: נהרי נחלי דבש (Job 20:17)." "<b>נבערה.</b> From the root of ואני בער (Psalms 73:22)." "<b>בן חכמים אני.</b> Like בן חורים (Ecclesiastes 10:17), for each man praises himself, (for) my father was wise and my ancestors too were kings in ancient days."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:17.462170798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}